                <pb facs="0254" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/211c</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-11-03T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1917, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1827. For Stevens [from Willard]:</p>
                <p>Following cable from American Consul, Tiflis, Caucasus: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Railroad conditions are deplorable and threaten famine consequence of
                            which the Consul recommends urgently that our railway commission send an
                            expert to study problem. The authorities in the Caucasus are reported to
                            be most anxious for assistance. The chief of the British Military
                            Mission, General Shore, seems to be doubtful of possibility of holding
                            the army on that front unless conditions of railroad transportation
                            improve.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>What do you think can be done? You know the kind of forces we are sending with
                    Emerson. What if anything else do you think we ought to do to meet the condition
                    in the south of Russia?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
